  "title": "HELP! The Ask a Manager blog is everywhere!",
  "summary": "I have muted (super-disliked) Ask a Manager by title, author, category and URL. And yet it continues to show up in both Widely Read and Long Reads feeds unabated. Relatedly, at a philosophical level, I think it is a problem that a handful of blogs dominate both these categories. I can see why that makes sense for widely read (people love office gossip?) but I don’t think Ask a Manager should qualify as a long read. I don’t think it would ever be selected on longform.org or longreads.org.",
